      <string id="General_Enabled">Enable the cleanup engine</string>
      <string id="General_Enabled_Help">When disabled, every run ends at once with result Disabled and changes nothing.

Enabled sets 1, Disabled sets 0. Shipped default: Enabled (1).

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad, value Enabled (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="General_ReportOnly">Report only (change nothing)</string>
      <string id="General_ReportOnly_Help">Runs scan and plan every category and log what would be done, without deleting, compressing, copying or moving anything.

Enabled sets 1, Disabled sets 0. Shipped default: Disabled (0).

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad, value ReportOnly (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="General_TimeBudgetMinutes">Time budget per run (minutes)</string>
      <string id="General_TimeBudgetMinutes_Help">A run stops cleanly between items when this time is used; the result is Partial.

Allowed values: 1 to 600. Shipped default: 20.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad, value TimeBudgetMinutes (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="General_MaxDeleteMBPerRun">Maximum megabytes acted on per run</string>
      <string id="General_MaxDeleteMBPerRun_Help">0 means no limit.

Allowed values: 0 to 10000000. Shipped default: 0.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad, value MaxDeleteMBPerRun (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="General_MaxItemsPerRun">Maximum items acted on per run</string>
      <string id="General_MaxItemsPerRun_Help">0 means no limit.

Allowed values: 0 to 10000000. Shipped default: 100000.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad, value MaxItemsPerRun (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="General_UseLastAccess">Use last access time as activity</string>
      <string id="General_UseLastAccess_Help">When enabled and NTFS records last access, a file read recently counts as active. Disable where scanners or backup inflate last access.

Enabled sets 1, Disabled sets 0. Shipped default: Enabled (1).

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad, value UseLastAccess (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="General_LogRetentionDays">Keep run logs (days)</string>
      <string id="General_LogRetentionDays_Help">Run logs and run reports older than this are removed from the data folder.

Allowed values: 1 to 3650. Shipped default: 90.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad, value LogRetentionDays (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="General_OnDemandMode">What a user-requested cleanup runs</string>
      <string id="General_OnDemandMode_Help">The OnDemand task, which users may start, runs this mode. It takes no input from the user.

Allowed values: Maintenance, PressureCheck. Shipped default: Maintenance.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad, value OnDemandMode (REG_SZ). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Value_Maintenance">Maintenance</string>
      <string id="Value_PressureCheck">PressureCheck</string>
      <string id="Pressure_FloorPercent">Pressure floor (percent free)</string>
      <string id="Pressure_FloorPercent_Help">Below the floor (the larger of the percent and GB values, in bytes) pressure tiers run until the target is reached.

Allowed values: 0 to 90. Shipped default: 5.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Pressure) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Pressure, value FloorPercent (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Pressure_FloorGB">Pressure floor (GB free)</string>
      <string id="Pressure_FloorGB_Help">See the floor percent setting.

Allowed values: 0 to 100000. Shipped default: 30.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Pressure) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Pressure, value FloorGB (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Pressure_TargetPercent">Pressure target (percent free)</string>
      <string id="Pressure_TargetPercent_Help">Pressure tiers stop as soon as free space reaches the larger of the percent and GB values.

Allowed values: 0 to 95. Shipped default: 8.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Pressure) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Pressure, value TargetPercent (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Pressure_TargetGB">Pressure target (GB free)</string>
      <string id="Pressure_TargetGB_Help">See the target percent setting.

Allowed values: 0 to 100000. Shipped default: 45.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Pressure) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Pressure, value TargetGB (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Schedule_MaintenanceDays">Maintenance days</string>
      <string id="Schedule_MaintenanceDays_Help">Comma-separated day names, for example Sunday or Monday,Thursday.

Format: comma-separated English day names (Sunday to Saturday). Shipped default: Sunday.

