Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Schedule, value MaintenanceDays (REG_SZ). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Schedule_MaintenanceTime">Maintenance time (HH:mm)</string>
      <string id="Schedule_MaintenanceTime_Help">Local time. A missed run starts when the machine is next available.

Format: HH:mm, 24-hour local time. Shipped default: 03:00.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Schedule) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Schedule, value MaintenanceTime (REG_SZ). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Schedule_PressureCheckTime">Daily pressure check time (HH:mm)</string>
      <string id="Schedule_PressureCheckTime_Help">The pressure check also runs on low disk events.

Format: HH:mm, 24-hour local time. Shipped default: 12:30.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Schedule) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Schedule, value PressureCheckTime (REG_SZ). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Schedule_RunOnlyIfIdle">Run maintenance only when idle</string>
      <string id="Schedule_RunOnlyIfIdle_Help">Adds an idle condition to the Maintenance task.

Enabled sets 1, Disabled sets 0. Shipped default: Disabled (0).

