      <string id="Schedule_AllowOnBattery">Allow runs on battery</string>
      <string id="Schedule_AllowOnBattery_Help">Off: scheduled runs do not start on battery power.

Enabled sets 1, Disabled sets 0. Shipped default: Disabled (0).

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Schedule) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Schedule, value AllowOnBattery (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Tray_ShowTray">Show the tray app</string>
      <string id="Tray_ShowTray_Help">Off: the tray app exits at start.

Enabled sets 1, Disabled sets 0. Shipped default: Enabled (1).

Not configured: the user policy applies, else the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Tray), else the shipped default. Machine policy takes precedence over user policy.

Registry: HKLM or HKCU\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Tray, value ShowTray (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Tray_AllowCleanTemp">Allow &quot;Clean my temp files&quot;</string>
      <string id="Tray_AllowCleanTemp_Help">Users may delete their own eligible temp files.

Enabled sets 1, Disabled sets 0. Shipped default: Enabled (1).

Not configured: the user policy applies, else the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Tray), else the shipped default. Machine policy takes precedence over user policy.

Registry: HKLM or HKCU\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Tray, value AllowCleanTemp (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Tray_AllowRequestCleanup">Allow &quot;Request a cleanup&quot;</string>
      <string id="Tray_AllowRequestCleanup_Help">Users may start the OnDemand task.

Enabled sets 1, Disabled sets 0. Shipped default: Enabled (1).

Not configured: the user policy applies, else the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Tray), else the shipped default. Machine policy takes precedence over user policy.

