Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Categories\windows.temp, value PressureTier (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Category_windows_temp_PressureAction">windows.temp: Pressure action</string>
      <string id="Category_windows_temp_PressureAction_Help">Category windows.temp.

What happens to items given up under pressure.

Allowed values: Delete, Compress, Copy, Move. Shipped default: Delete.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Categories\windows.temp) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Categories\windows.temp, value PressureAction (REG_SZ). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Category_windows_temp_PressureAgeDays">windows.temp: Pressure minimum age (days)</string>
      <string id="Category_windows_temp_PressureAgeDays_Help">Category windows.temp.

Only items older than this are given up under pressure.

Allowed values: 0 to 36500. Shipped default: 1.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Categories\windows.temp) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Categories\windows.temp, value PressureAgeDays (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="Category_windows_temp_PressureKeepNewest">windows.temp: Pressure keeps newest (count)</string>
      <string id="Category_windows_temp_PressureKeepNewest_Help">Category windows.temp.

The newest items of each group are kept under pressure.

Allowed values: 0 to 1000000. Shipped default: 0.

Not configured: the local setting (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\Categories\windows.temp) applies, else the shipped default.

Registry: HKLM\Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Categories\windows.temp, value PressureKeepNewest (REG_DWORD). A value the engine cannot use is ignored (event 3002) and the next source applies.</string>
      <string id="CustomTargets">Custom targets</string>
      <string id="CustomTargets_Help">Adds cleanup targets beyond the built-in categories. Each entry is one registry value under Software\Policies\DeadLoad\CustomTargets: the value name is the target name and the value data is its definition. Policy entries take precedence over local entries (HKLM\Software\DeadLoad\CustomTargets) of the same name.

Value name: 1 to 64 characters (letters, digits, period, underscore, hyphen), starting with a letter or digit. The target becomes category custom.&lt;name&gt;; its settings can be tuned under Software\Policies\DeadLoad\Categories\custom.&lt;name&gt; like a built-in category.

Value data: semicolon-separated fields, for example:
Path={LocalAppData}\Example\Logs;Include=*.log;Unit=File;AgeDays=30;Action=Delete

Path (required): a folder template that starts with an allowed root. Backslashes only; .. is not allowed.
Include: comma-separated file name patterns (default *).
Unit: File or Folder (default File).
AgeDays: items whose activity is older than this many days are selected; at least 1 unless Action is None.
Action: Delete, Compress, Copy, Move or None (default Delete).
Recurse: 1 to include subfolders (default 0).

Allowed roots:
{LocalAppData}
{Temp}
{WindowsTemp}
{SystemDrive}\Autodesk
{ProgramData}\Autodesk

Protected paths and protected file types still apply. A target that breaks these rules is ignored (event 3002) and the others still run.</string>
    </stringTable>
